lueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-zero</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-no-conjugate-ball</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-1-exp-norm-transfer-mfderiv</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23lem%3Adc-ch8-2-2-semiconjugacy\">↗ lem:dc-ch8-2-2-semiconjugacy</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch8:2.3</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> be a space of constant curvature and let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span> be any two points of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span>. Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ e_j\\} $\">$\\{ e_j\\} $</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\{ f_j\\} $\">$\\{ f_j\\} $</span> be arbitrary orthonormal bases of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_p(M)$\">$T_p(M)$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_q(M)$\">$T_q(M)$</span>, respectively. Then there exist neighborhoods <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$U$\">$U$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p$\">$p$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$V$\">$V$</span> of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$q$\">$q$</span>, and an isometry <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$g:U\\to V$\">$g:U\\to V$</span> such that <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$dg_p(e_j)=f_j$\">$dg_p(e_j)=f_j$</span>. <p></p> <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23cor%3Adc-ch8-2-2\">↗ cor:dc-ch8-2-2</a> \\sketch Apply <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature%23cor%3Adc-ch8-2-2\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#cor:dc-ch8-2-2\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-636f723a64632d6368382d322d32\">item 3</a> with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde M=M$\">$\\tilde M=M$</span> and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\tilde p=q$\">$\\tilde p=q$</span>, taking for <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$i$\">$i$</span> the linear isometry <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$T_pM\\to T_qM$\">$T_pM\\to T_qM$</span> carrying <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$e_j$\">$e_j$</span> to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$f_j$\">$f_j$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#cor:dc-ch8-2-2","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#def:dc-ch8-3-hyperbolic-space","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch08_SpacesOfConstantCurvature#lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer-const","title":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer-const","label":"lem:dc-ch8-2-1-jacobi-transfer-const"},{"ki